  ($t$LAW25.3.1.1-L0-0$t$, $t$Governance & Accountability$t$, $t$GOV$t$, $t$LAW25.3.1.1$t$, $t$Has the organization identified the person in charge of the protection of personal information (by default the person exercising the highest authority), and is any delegation of that function made in writing?$t$, $t$Act respecting the protection of personal information in the private sector (CQLR c. P-39.1), s. 3.1$t$, 0),
  ($t$LAW25.3.1.2-L0-1$t$, $t$Governance & Accountability$t$, $t$GOV$t$, $t$LAW25.3.1.2$t$, $t$Are the title and contact information of the person in charge of the protection of personal information published on the organization's website, or made available by another appropriate means if it has no website?$t$, $t$Act respecting the protection of personal information in the private sector (CQLR c. P-39.1), s. 3.1$t$, 1),
  ($t$LAW25.3.2.1-L0-2$t$, $t$Governance & Accountability$t$, $t$GOV$t$, $t$LAW25.3.2.1$t$, $t$Has the organization established and implemented governance policies and practices for personal information that are proportionate to the nature and scale of its activities and approved by the person in charge?$t$, $t$Act respecting the protection of personal information in the private sector (CQLR c. P-39.1), s. 3.2$t$, 2),
  ($t$LAW25.3.2.2-L0-3$t$, $t$Governance & Accountability$t$, $t$GOV$t$, $t$LAW25.3.2.2$t$, $t$Do the governance policies and practices provide a framework for keeping and destroying personal information, define the roles and responsibilities of personnel throughout the information life cycle, and provide a process for handling complaints?$t$, $t$Act respecting the protection of personal information in the private sector (CQLR c. P-39.1), s. 3.2$t$, 3),
  ($t$LAW25.3.2.3-L0-4$t$, $t$Governance & Accountability$t$, $t$GOV$t$, $t$LAW25.3.2.3$t$, $t$Is detailed information about these policies and practices published in simple and clear language on the organization's website?$t$, $t$Act respecting the protection of personal information in the private sector (CQLR c. P-39.1), s. 3.2$t$, 4),
  ($t$LAW25.20-L0-5$t$, $t$Governance & Accountability$t$, $t$GOV$t$, $t$LAW25.20$t$, $t$Is access to personal information within the organization limited to the employees and agents for whom it is necessary for the performance of their duties?$t$, $t$Act respecting the protection of personal information in the private sector (CQLR c. P-39.1), s. 20$t$, 5),
  ($t$LAW25.3.3.1-L0-6$t$, $t$Privacy Impact Assessments$t$, $t$PIA$t$, $t$LAW25.3.3.1$t$, $t$Does the organization conduct a privacy impact assessment for any project to acquire, develop or overhaul an information system or electronic service delivery system involving personal information?$t$, $t$Act respecting the protection of personal information in the private sector (CQLR c. P-39.1), s. 3.3$t$, 6),
  ($t$LAW25.3.3.2-L0-7$t$, $t$Privacy Impact Assessments$t$, $t$PIA$t$, $t$LAW25.3.3.2$t$, $t$Is the person in charge of the protection of personal information consulted from the outset of such projects, and is each assessment proportionate to the sensitivity, purpose, quantity, distribution and medium of the information?$t$, $t$Act respecting the protection of personal information in the private sector (CQLR c. P-39.1), s. 3.3$t$, 7),
